1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,825
Sports Technology Revolution Reshapes Training and Fan Experience.

2
00:00:04,775 --> 00:00:16,025
The integration of artificial intelligence and data analytics into professional sports reached a new peak in 2026, transforming everything from athlete training to in-stadium fan engagement.

3
00:00:16,025 --> 00:00:28,800
The World Cup's expanded 104-match schedule served as a showcase for AI-powered player tracking, with FIFA's semi-automated offside technology achieving 99.7% accuracy on offside calls.

4
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:41,450
In the NBA, all 30 franchises now employ dedicated machine learning engineers, with teams using computer vision to analyze biomechanics and reduce injury risk by an estimated 22% league-wide.

5
00:00:41,450 --> 00:00:56,562
Fan-facing technology also advanced rapidly: augmented reality overlays at arenas and stadiums provided real-time player statistics and replays through smartphone cameras, while AI-generated highlight packages personalized content for individual viewers.

6
00:00:56,562 --> 00:01:08,712
The wearable sensor market for athletes surpassed $4 billion in annual revenue, with smart compression garments and implantable microchips monitoring hydration, fatigue, and muscle strain in real time.

7
00:01:08,712 --> 00:01:23,187
Sports betting platforms integrated live AI odds adjusted by micro-movements on the field, creating a more dynamic experience for the estimated 65 million Americans who wagered legally during the 2025-26 sports calendar.

